<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Da Gama interim shr, div slips.</title>
<headline>Da Gama interim shr, div slips.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	   21.6	  vs  29.4</p>
<p>    Shr, cash equivalent	37.9	  vs  45.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			7.0	  vs   9.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income		 11.03	 vs  14.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			 13.62	 vs  21.39</p>
<p>    Tax				2.59	 vs   6.42</p>
<p>    Interest earned		4.81	 vs   3.39</p>
<p>    Turnover		     142.21	 vs 166.95</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 31</p>
<p>on register Nov 29</p>
<p>Full name: Da Gama Textile Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that in the current environment, volumes and profit margins were unlikely to improve in the second half. It added that accordingly a further decrease in comparative earnings can be expected in the remaining six months of the financial year, despite a reasonable forward order book over three months' sales.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
